# The approach and the landing in a business jet.
#
#   name TEXT...                   what the lesson is called
#   teaches CLASS                  which class of aircraft it is for
#   stage TEXT...                  a stage, in the order flown
#   do TEXT...                     what to do at this stage
#   until PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE     what ends the stage
#   hold PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT... a band that must hold for the whole stage
#   need PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE TEXT...  what must be true by the stage's end
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/lesson.hpp owns the format.
#
# **Every speed is `vref`**, the aeroplane own threshold speed, worked out by
# `sim::approach_speeds` as 1.3 times its published stall with everything
# down. Writing a number would hold one aeroplane to another speed.
#
# **No band watches the flare**, as in the light aircraft lesson: the flare is
# where the speed is meant to go.
#
# **A jet begins its flare higher than a light aeroplane**, which is why the
# speed is watched down to forty feet here and to twenty in the light aircraft
# lesson. The Learjet crosses its threshold at about 125 knots and is down to
# 95 by twenty feet: that is the flare doing its work, not an approach flown
# slow, and a band that watched it would fault every correct landing the
# aeroplane makes.

name Approach and landing in a business jet
teaches business-jet

stage The approach
do Join the approach on the runway heading, wheels and flap down
do Hold the approach speed and let her come down the glidepath
hold velocities/vc-kts vref-8 vref+15 Hold the approach speed
until position/h-agl-ft <= 50

stage Over the threshold
do Cross the threshold at the approach speed, on the centreline
hold velocities/vc-kts vref-8 vref+15 Cross the threshold on speed
until position/h-agl-ft <= 40

stage The flare and the landing roll
do Close the throttles and check the descent
do Hold her straight, and brake once she is rolling
need fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.15 Close the throttles for the landing
until velocities/vc-kts <= 30
